cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TLD Abuse Intelligence: Phishing, Payload Delivery, and C2 Infrastructure"
message: "If you use this dataset or analysis, please cite it and note the snapshot date, as the data is refreshed continuously."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "jejex0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jejex0/tld-abuse-intel"
url: "https://github.com/jejex0/tld-abuse-intel"
license: MIT
version: "2026.11.02"
date-released: "2026-11-02"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, source-attributed ranking of top-level domains by their
  concentration of phishing, payload/staging, and command-and-control abuse.
  Combines live feeds, annual registry studies (2020-2026), and Internet Archive
  history into a four-tier risk model with an independent evidence-confidence
  score and a blocklist-suitability assessment.
keywords:
  - threat intelligence
  - phishing
  - DNS security
  - top-level domains
  - command and control
  - malware
  - blocklist
